    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters May 15th with a primary objective of chasing stolen bases while exploiting soft matchups. **Corbin Carroll** (78.80) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) represent our highest efficiency ceiling today. Both benefit from a premium park factor (+14%) and a favorable matchup against Freeland and Kelly, respectively. **Mickey Moniak** specifically draws a massive +14% boost from his platoon advantage and benefits from Kelly\u2019s lack of urgency in the delivery, providing a green light for his speed profile. **Josh Naylor** (73.26) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) round out the core, both capitalizing on sub-5.00 xERA opposing arms, with **Josh Naylor** serving as our most reliable run-production anchor in the three-hole. **James Wood** remains a must-start at 68.08; despite facing the tougher Baz, his leadoff spot (+10% order bonus) and 0.380 xwOBA make him a primary engine for our R/SB production.\n\nRegarding roster management, the toughest exclusion today was **Austin Riley** (44.09), who fell just shy of the starting threshold. While his talent is clear, he is neutralized by a difficult matchup against Early (2.92 xERA) and negative SP skill adjustments, making him a high-risk play compared to the efficiency provided by **Gabriel Moreno** or **Dalton Rushing**. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Brice Turang** (56.96). While his baseline is solid, his score is bolstered by a +5% wind-out factor and an advantageous #2 spot in the order. We are proceeding with our current configuration, though the team remains cautious about the bottom of the order; specifically, **Cole Young** (46.64) and **Zach McKinstry** (44.55) are operating at our absolute floor for starts today. We are effectively punting bench depth while **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined, prioritizing game cap preservation over speculative pinch-hit opportunities from **Travis Bazzana**.",
